  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">INTERNATIONAL FERTILIZER DEVELOPMENT CENTER</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to eliminate hunger and to reduce poverty among households in the targeted population of Nyandarua County. It aims to achieve this through increasing smallholder farmers&#x2019; incomes from potato production through improved production practices, reduction of post-harvest losses, introducing improved potato varieties and linking farmers to reliable markets. In 2024, the project will consolidate lessons learned since 2017 through policy and communication activities, dialogue with regional and national stakeholders on implementation of potato regulations, an end-term evaluation and other close-out activities, including the finalisation of a potato storage facility. The Embassy will provide technical advice and oversight to ensure the responsible close-out of the project and the partnership.</narrative>
  </description>
